[Business Size (FTE)]
- Business size measured in Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) is a metric that standardizes a company's total workforce size by converting all employee work hours into the equivalent number of full-time workers

- FTE = Full-Time Equivalent.

- FTE = Total hours worked by employee / standard full time hours
  - For example:
    - The standard full-time schedule is 40 hours/week
    - 10 employees working 40 hours/week → 400 hours
    - 4 employees working 20 hours/week → 80 hours
    - Then, FTE = (400 + 80) / 40 = 480 / 40 = 12 FTE
    - This means, those 14 people represent 12 full-time equivalents.

- [ ] Question the company:
